# Files where prettier is not the right owner of the formatting.
#
# Two distinct reasons appear below, and each entry states its own. This is not a general licence to
# silence the formatter: a file belongs here only when prettier's output is either DISCARDED by
# something else or actively COSTLY, and the cost is measurable. Everything else stays formatted --
# `make prettier-check` is the whole point, and CI runs prettier over changed files on every PR.

# --- Reason 1: a generator writes it, so prettier's opinion is overwritten anyway. ---

# Written by `python3 dev/tests/invariants-gate.py --update-baseline` (json.dumps indent=2).
# Prettier collapses single-element arrays onto one line; json.dumps never does, so the two
# reformat each other forever and every run of either shows up as a diff nobody wrote. Nothing else
# about the file is contested, and the ratchet reads it with `json.load`, which does not care.
dev/assertion-baseline.json

# --- Reason 2: table padding is 50-64% of a file the harness reads on EVERY invocation. ---
#
# Prettier pads each table cell out to the widest cell in its column. On a table whose widest cell
# is a 3 KB paragraph, every other row in that column is padded to 3 KB of trailing spaces. These
# two files are mandated reading at ORIENT, and the padding alone had made LEDGER.md too large for a
# single `Read`: 446 KB in 414 lines, of which 287 KB was whitespace. LESSONS.md was 160 KB, 53%
# padding.
#
# The fix is not "run prettier less often" -- it is that these two files pay a real per-invocation
# context cost for an alignment nobody reads, so the formatter does not get a vote. Write table rows
# with single spaces around the pipes; nothing will re-pad them. LESSONS.md went further and turned
# its per-lesson tables into bold-label prose, which prettier could not have padded either way.
#
# Both files were ALREADY failing `make prettier-check` on main before this, so listing them here
# fixes that target rather than papering over it.
docs/build/LEDGER.md
.claude/harness/LESSONS.md
# The archive is the moved half of LEDGER.md and was de-padded in the same pass. Left out, prettier
# would re-pad it on the next run and hand back the 290 KB the move just removed.
docs/build/archive/LEDGER-phases-0-7.md

# --- Reason 3: the file's malformation IS the fixture. ---
#
# verification/fixtures/envelopes/malformed/ is the negative corpus the broker's decoder is tested
# against. Two of them are not parseable JSON at all -- a truncated document, and two JSON values
# concatenated -- so prettier exits with a SyntaxError and fails `prettier --check` over the branch
# diff. Formatting the rest is worse than useless: several assert a property of the BYTES (a
# duplicate key, a specific escape, trailing content after the value), and a formatter that
# round-trips them through a parser repairs the exact defect the fixture exists to carry, leaving a
# test that passes while asserting nothing.
verification/fixtures/envelopes/malformed/
